{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"76842aac814a677f","type":"text","text":"## Title\nThroughput-Optimal Scheduling Algorithms for LLM Inference and AI Agents\n## Abstract\n随着对大语言模型 (LLM) 和 AI 智能体的需求迅速增长，优化系统以实现高效的 LLM 推理变得至关重要。 虽然大量工作都针对系统级工程，但通过数学建模和排队论的角度进行的研究很少。\n\n在本文中，我们旨在发展 LLM 推理的排队论基础，弥合排队论和 LLM 系统社区之间的差距。 特别地，我们研究了 LLM 推理系统的吞吐量方面。 我们证明，一大类“保工”调度算法可以实现单个请求和 AI 智能体工作负载的最大吞吐量，突出了“保工”作为实践中的关键设计原则。 对现实世界系统的评估表明，Orca 和 Sarathi-serve 是吞吐量最优的，这使实践者放心，而 FastTransformer 和普通 vLLM 则不是最大稳定性，应谨慎使用。 我们的结果突出了排队论社区在分析和改进 LLM 推理系统方面可以提供的巨大好处，并呼吁进行更多跨学科发展。 \n## Summary\n提出将forward时间和处理的token数量成正比的关系\n将调度算法使用Markov Chain进行formulate\n## Links\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07347\nhttps://yiyibooks.cn/arxiv/2504.07347v1/index.html\n## Cite\n```\n@misc{li2025throughputoptimalschedulingalgorithmsllm,\n      title={Throughput-Optimal Scheduling Algorithms for LLM Inference and AI Agents}, \n      author={Yueying Li and Jim Dai and Tianyi Peng},\n      year={2025},\n      eprint={2504.07347},\n      archivePrefix={arXiv},\n      primaryClass={stat.ML},\n      url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07347}, \n}\n```","x":-480,"y":-40,"width":680,"height":860},
		{"id":"6661864413b57542","type":"file","file":"Agent/Asserts/20250502213451451.png","x":1530,"y":-480,"width":980,"height":380},
		{"id":"26d2c340fdd96599","type":"text","text":"Figure 1: Visualization of key scheduling terminologies in LLM engine.","x":1734,"y":-80,"width":572,"height":50},
		{"id":"70f734c5d4d50273","type":"file","file":"Agent/Asserts/20250505150540475.png","x":1585,"y":90,"width":870,"height":713},
		{"id":"1af462f98a3be7aa","type":"text","text":"## 马尔可夫链(Markov Chain)\n**马尔可夫链**是一种**随机过程**，用来描述一个系统在不同状态之间随机转换的过程\n### 性质\n**马尔可夫性质（Markov Property）**：  \n系统的**下一状态**只依赖于当前状态，而**与过去的状态无关**。\n$$\n\\mathbb{P}(X_{n + 1} = x_{n + 1} \\mid X_{n} = x_{n}, X_{n - 1} = x_{n - 1}, \\dots, X_{1} = x_{1}) = \\mathbb{P}(X_{n + 1} = x_{n + 1} \\mid X_{n} = x_{n})\n$$","x":290,"y":-720,"width":660,"height":320},
		{"id":"af8ed56bd6afc78d","type":"text","text":"Tensor model parallelism (TP)  (Narayanan et al., 2021) distributes computations across GPUs by partitioning transformer weight matrices row-wise and column-wise, with layer outputs aggregated through two AllReduce operations.\n\nThe state-of-the-art LLM serving systems currently leverage an optimization technique known as continuous batching (Yu et al., 2022), which combines new request prefill operations with ongoing request decoding operations in the same batch to improve GPU utilization, making batching decisions at the token level.","x":400,"y":-200,"width":660,"height":460},
		{"id":"53cbce867cf20ffe","type":"text","text":"时间： $n \\in \\mathbb{N} \\equiv \\{1, 2, \\dots\\}$\n时间段n到达系统的请求数：  $a_n$\n请求编号：i=1,2,3,...\n请求i的prefill-tokens：$v_p(i) \\in \\mathbb{N}$\n请求i的decode-tokens：$v_d(i) \\in \\mathbb{N}$\n请求i的特征：$z(i) \\in \\mathcal{K}$\n","x":480,"y":480,"width":440,"height":177}
